Define rules that tensorflow.raw_ops.Greater API parameters should satisfy. Refer to the API documentation. 

Type is encoded as an integer (index of the following list):
[bool, np.int8, np.int16, np.int32, np.int64, np.uint8, np.float16, np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128, str, np.dtype]

String value should be selected from the following list:
["ii", "ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba", "none", "sum", "max", "min", "prod", "relu", "tanh", "sigmoid", "softmax", "elu", "selu", "gelu", "swish", "softplus", "linear", "valid", "same", "causal", "channels_last", "channels_first"]

[API Documentation]
Returns the truth value of (x > y) element-wise.

  *NOTE*: `math.greater` supports broadcasting. More about broadcasting
  [here](http://docs.scipy.org/doc/numpy/user/basics.broadcasting.html)

  Example:

  ```python
  x = tf.constant([5, 4, 6])
  y = tf.constant([5, 2, 5])
  tf.math.greater(x, y) ==> [False, True, True]

  x = tf.constant([5, 4, 6])
  y = tf.constant([5])
  tf.math.greater(x, y) ==> [False, False, True]
  ```

  Args:
    x: A `Tensor`. Must be one of the following types: `float32`, `float64`, `int32`, `uint8`, `int16`, `int8`, `int64`, `bfloat16`, `uint16`, `half`, `uint32`, `uint64`.
    y: A `Tensor`. Must have the same type as `x`.
    name: A name for the operation (optional).

  Returns:
    A `Tensor` of type `bool`.

[API Signature] name: string, x: tensor, y: tensor

